camchrome: a macOS persona's text scaler, raster scale and WebGPU canvas format.

The macOS persona's first Clearcote audit flagged five signals. Three are fixed here:
  * text: a 0.01 px font-size step changed the width on 126 of 200 steps, FreeType's 26.6 grid;
    CoreText advances continuously, so the float advances of 1018/1021 now apply to macOS too
    (without DirectWrite's 16-level coverage ladder);
  * raster scale: devicePixelRatio 2 rasterised at 1x (a 100 px box measured 100 device pixels,
    srcset picked the 1x image); 1017's forced scale now covers a macOS persona, exactly 2.
    tools/persona_display.py sizes the X screen at that scale;
  * WebGPU: getPreferredCanvasFormat() said rgba8unorm, the Linux answer; Chrome on macOS
    prefers bgra8unorm, as 970 already reports for Windows.
Still open, and not guessed: Math.tanh (Apple's libm bits are not public, and a third value
matches no real OS) and the CPU architecture (an x86 host's quiet-NaN sign bit beside an Apple
Silicon "arm" claim). Both need a real Mac to record from.

--- a/chrome/app/chrome_main_delegate.cc
+++ b/chrome/app/chrome_main_delegate.cc
@@ -1268,6 +1268,12 @@
     setenv("CAMCHROME_FT_FLOAT_ADVANCES", "1", /*overwrite=*/0);
     setenv("CAMCHROME_FT_COVERAGE_LEVELS", "16", /*overwrite=*/0);
   }
+  // camchrome (1025): and as CoreText advances them for a macOS persona (continuous advances;
+  // the coverage ladder is DirectWrite's alone).
+  if (persona_browser_process && ungoogled::PersonaActive() &&
+      ungoogled::GetPersonaPlatform() == ungoogled::PersonaPlatform::kMacOS) {
+    setenv("CAMCHROME_FT_FLOAT_ADVANCES", "1", /*overwrite=*/0);
+  }
 
   // camchrome (1008): browser-process defaults that make a persona true rather than reported.
   // Children copy both switches from the browser's command line.
@@ -1294,7 +1300,10 @@
       // device pixel of 100 x dpr (as a fractional-ratio display rounds), and the reported
       // devicePixelRatio stays the persona's. Needs an X screen of the phone's size at that
       // scale; tools/persona_display.py starts one. An explicit scale factor wins.
-      if (persona.mobile && persona.screen_width > 0 &&
+      // camchrome (1025): a macOS persona's Retina ratio too (whole, so exactly 2).
+      const bool camchrome_mac_persona =
+          ungoogled::GetPersonaPlatform() == ungoogled::PersonaPlatform::kMacOS;
+      if ((persona.mobile || camchrome_mac_persona) && persona.screen_width > 0 &&
           persona.device_pixel_ratio > 1.0 &&
           !cmd->HasSwitch(switches::kForceDeviceScaleFactor)) {
         const double physical =
